# Lingotorte environment template. Placeholders only: never commit real values.
#
# Docker (primary): compose.yaml sets service host/port, data roots and
# LINGOTORTE_ALLOW_ONLINE_PROVIDERS=false itself, and .dockerignore keeps env
# files out of the image. You normally need only these shell variables when
# running `docker compose` (see docs/dev/docker-runbook.md):
#   LINGOTORTE_MEDIA_DIR=<absolute owned-media directory>
#   LINGOTORTE_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1
#   LINGOTORTE_WEB_PORT=5173
#   LINGOTORTE_PUBLIC_ORIGINS=http://127.0.0.1:5173
#
# Direct (non-Docker) runs: data defaults to %LOCALAPPDATA%\lingotorte on
# Windows and $XDG_DATA_HOME/lingotorte or ~/.local/share/lingotorte on Linux.
# Set LINGOTORTE_DATA_DIR only to override that with an absolute native path.
# LINGOTORTE_DATA_DIR=

# Online providers are off by default and need explicit opt-in per
# DECISIONS.md §6. Keep provider keys in a file OUTSIDE this checkout, e.g.
# %LOCALAPPDATA%\lingotorte\provider.env. `npm run scan:privacy` fails if a
# .env file in the checkout holds a non-empty *_KEY/TOKEN/SECRET/PASSWORD.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# LINGOTORTE_ALLOW_ONLINE_PROVIDERS=false
